From: Ze kernel maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] ppp: validate original creator files for link and address writes

Based on Linux v7.3 and Ze's preceding registered kernel patches.

An explicit creator-only PPPIOCGOWNER validates the live original struct file
and expected unit/index in the caller namespace. Its feature reply advertises
only RTM_SETLINK MTU/IFF_UP and IPv4/IPv6 address guards. It advertises NO route
guard. Route guards are introduced by the following patch.

The optional signed descriptor attributes require a positive ABI reply first:
old kernels can ignore unknown attributes. Guarded link NEWLINK/DELLINK and
unsupported SETLINK forms refuse. A duplicate of the creator file is valid;
a separately opened PPPIOCATTACH file is not. Hold fget across the native
writer, validate under RTNL without ppp_mutex, and fput after unlocking.

